<title>USA: Summit Bancorp completes Collective buy.</title>
<headline>Summit Bancorp completes Collective buy.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summit Bancorp said Friday it has  completed its acquisition of Collective Bancorp Inc.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the deal, the exchange ratio will be 0.895 share  of Summit common stock for each share of Collective Bancorp common  stock in a tax-free exchange. Shareholders of Collective will be receiving  additional information regarding the exchange of shares.</p>
<p>Collective Bancorp is a thrift holding company with $5.5 billion in  assets, and through its subsidiary, Collective Bank operates 82 branches  in 15 counties throughout New Jersey.</p>
</text>
